These tutorials have been recently updated to run with the latest GeN-Foam
on the branch developSRFFS. The main difference consists in a revamped 
thermal-hydraulics, now entirely based on the FFSEulerFoam multi-phase
solver (private repository at https://gitlab.com/virmodoetiae/FFSEulerFoam,
contact Stefan Radman, stefan.radman@epfl.ch or Carlo Fiorina,
carlo.fiorina@epfl.ch for info). 

The single-phase or two-phase thermal-hydraulic variants are run time
selectable (just like neutronics models). Examples on the single-phase variant
are found in 2D_onePhaseAndPointKineticsCoupling, 3D_MSFR, 3D_SmallESFR.
Examples of the two-phase variant are found in 1D_boilingNoRegimeMap and 
2D_voidMotionNoPhaseChange. The most commented inputs are currently found in
1D_boilingNoRegimeMap, yet these tutorials are not in their final form and are
still susceptible to updates. The 2D_RegressionESFR is the last tutorial that
needs to be updated to be compatible with the latest GeN-Foam; it will take
some time due to its complexity.

While the original GeN-Foam thermal-hydraulics and the new one have a
significant amount of differences, for the time being, the most immediate ones
are:

-	the U field now represents the REAL fluid velocity, not the superficial
	one! Be mindful of this when setting boundary conditions

-	the volumeFraction keyword to be specified in the phasePropertiesDict
	(i.e. the dict that substitues porousMediumProperties and fuelProperties)
	represents the volume fraction of the porous structure and is the 
	opposite of what was previously known as voidFraction, i.e.
	volumeFraction = 1 - voidFraction
	
Needless to say, this is a stub and only the most vital/primary info with
respect to the changes is provided. This will be greatly expanded with the
provision of actual documentation in the coming months
